<article class="env-lemma" id="0AQ9">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0AQ9">Lemma <span data-tag="0AQ9">88.23.1</span>.</a> In the situation above. If $f$ is locally of finite type, then $f_{/T}$ is locally of finite type. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      (Finite type morphisms of formal algebraic spaces are discussed in Formal Spaces, Section <a href="/tag/0AM3" data-tag="0AM3">87.24</a>.) Namely, suppose that $Z \to X$ is a morphism from a scheme into $X$ such that $|Z|$ maps into $T$. From the cartesian square above we see that $Z \times _ X X'$ is an algebraic space representing $Z \times _{X_{/T}} X'_{/T'}$. Since $Z \times _ X X' \to Z$ is locally of finite type by Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/03XH" data-tag="03XH">67.23.3</a> we conclude. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>